---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout title="Accessibility Statement | CC3PO">
  <Header />
  <main class="legal-page">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Accessibility Statement</h1>
      <p class="last-updated">Last Updated: May 20, 2026</p>

      <div class="content">
        <p><strong>CC3PO LLC</strong> is committed to ensuring digital accessibility for people with disabilities. We continually improve the user experience for everyone and apply relevant accessibility standards.</p>

        <h2>1. Our Commitment</h2>
        <p>We are committed to making our website accessible to all users, including those with visual, auditory, physical, and cognitive disabilities. We strive to meet or exceed the requirements of:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2</strong> — Level AA conformance</li>
          <li><strong>Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA)</strong> — Title III requirements for public accommodations</li>
          <li><strong>California Online Accessibility Act</strong> — State accessibility requirements</li>
          <li><strong>Section 508</strong> — Federal accessibility standards (where applicable)</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. Accessibility Features</h2>
        <p>Our website includes the following accessibility features:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Semantic HTML structure for proper screen reader navigation</li>
          <li>Alt text for all meaningful images</li>
          <li>Keyboard navigation support throughout the site</li>
          <li>Color contrast ratios meeting WCAG 2.2 AA standards</li>
          <li>Responsive design for all screen sizes and devices</li>
          <li>Form labels and ARIA attributes for assistive technology</li>
          <li>Skip navigation links for keyboard users</li>
          <li>No content that flashes more than 3 times per second</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Known Limitations</h2>
        <p>Despite our best efforts, some accessibility limitations may exist:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Some third-party embedded content may not be fully accessible</li>
          <li>PDF documents may not be fully screen-reader compatible</li>
          <li>Video content may not have complete closed captions</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We are actively working to address these limitations and welcome feedback on how we can improve.</p>

        <h2>4. Ongoing Efforts</h2>
        <p>We continuously work to improve accessibility by:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Conducting regular automated and manual accessibility audits</li>
          <li>Testing with assistive technologies (screen readers, keyboard-only navigation)</li>
          <li>Training our team on accessibility best practices</li>
          <li>Monitoring for new accessibility standards and guidelines</li>
          <li>Remediating issues as they are identified</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Our Compliance Monitoring</h2>
        <p>As a compliance and monitoring company, we practice what we preach. Our own website is regularly scanned using our <a href="/audit/">free accessibility scanner</a> to identify and resolve WCAG issues.</p>

        <h2>6. Feedback & Contact</h2>
        <p>We welcome your feedback on the accessibility of our website. If you encounter accessibility barriers, please contact us:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:legal@cc3po.com">legal@cc3po.com</a></li>
          <li><strong>Phone:</strong> <a href="tel:+12097011137">(209) 701-1137</a></li>
          <li><strong>Mail:</strong> CC3PO LLC, 16299 Adobe Way, Lathrop, CA 95330</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We aim to respond to accessibility feedback within 2 business days and to propose a solution within 10 business days.</p>

        <h2>7. Conformance Status</h2>
        <p>The <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG21/Understanding/conformance.html">Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG)</a> defines requirements for designers and developers to improve accessibility for people with disabilities. It defines three levels of conformance: Level A, Level AA, and Level AAA. <strong>CC3PO is partially conformant with WCAG 2.2 Level AA.</strong> Partially conformant means that some parts of the content do not fully conform to the accessibility standard.</p>

        <h2>8. Related Policies</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a></li>
          <li><a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a></li>
          <li><a href="/sms-consent/">SMS Consent &amp; Disclosure</a></li>
          <li><a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    padding: 80px 0 60px;
    min-height: 60vh;
  }
  .legal-page h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .last-updated {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  .content h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: 32px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .content p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .content ul {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    padding-left: 24px;
  }
  .content li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .content a {
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>